# Secrets. `.env` holds the OpenRouter key, the Telegram bot token and the
# opencode client credentials; `.env.oc` holds the `opencode serve` password.
# Both are committed nowhere and their examples are the only `.env*` files that
# may be tracked -- the negations below exist so a future `.env.local` or
# `.env.prod` is ignored by default rather than by remembering.
.env
.env.oc
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.oc.example

# Machine state and scratch output.
*.egg-info/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
db/
.venv/
.omo/
.r2d2/
/tmp/
.codegraph
__pycache__/
*.pyc
